{
  "$comment": "Recorded by hand: Zed spawned an agent built on this module, and Claude drove the agent panel through macOS accessibility, so every click and keystroke reached Zed as a user's would. Replayed by zed_test.go. Do not edit; CONTRIBUTING.md says how to record another.",
  "scenario": "a load the agent could not serve, then one session through every kind of turn the panel drives",
  "note": "Zed restored a thread whose session the agent no longer had and was answered -32002. A new thread then carried the user's last model and verbose choices over with two session/set_config_option calls, received the slash commands the agent announced right after session/new, and ran eight prompts: plain text, a plan with tool calls and a diff, a permission the user allowed followed by a file read and write, a terminal that exited 3, a form elicitation the user answered, a turn stopped from the stop button, a prompt that was only an embedded file, and a turn the agent failed on purpose.",
